This repository is the reserved product home of Boussole Politique. It carries a
frozen reference implementation, its specifications, and the dry-run material
built on French parliamentary open data. It is a multi-licence repository.

The licence for each file is declared through REUSE.toml:

- EUPL-1.2: first-party software — the Rust workspace under `crates/`, the
  application host under `apps/`, the workspace manifests and the files under
  `.github/`;
- Apache-2.0: interoperability and test material — the executable scoring
  vectors, the registered methodology parameters, and the generic verification
  and dry-run harnesses under `scripts/` and `dry-run/scripts/`;
- CC-BY-4.0: editorial documentation, specifications, methodology analyses and
  first-party project records, including the evidence files under `proofs/`;
- MIT: the visual identity under `assets/brand/` and its generated derivatives,
  which keep the standing declaration in `assets/brand/LICENSE.md` while the
  trademark review is pending;
- LicenseRef-ThirdParty-Data: the Assemblée nationale source archives under
  `dry-run/data/` and the machine-readable outputs derived from them. That
  material keeps the terms of its producer. No first-party licence is granted
  over it, and none may be inferred from the declarations above.

Full licence texts are stored in LICENSES/.

No licence here grants any right over the names, logos or marks "Libre AI" and
"Boussole Politique".

The organization-wide licensing policy — scope, precedence, historical grants,
data and contribution rules — is the canonical one and is not restated here:
https://github.com/libre-ai/libre-ai/blob/main/LICENSING.md

Historical revisions previously published under MIT remain available under those
terms. No previous licence grant is withdrawn.
